# Git Commit Message Conventions

Follow the Conventional Commits format:

```
<type>(<scope>): <short summary>

<optional body>

<optional footer>
```

## Types

- ✨ `feat` — new feature
- 🐛 `fix` — bug fix
- ♻️ `refactor` — code change that isn't a fix or feature
- 📝 `docs` — documentation only
- 🧪 `test` — adding or updating tests
- 🔧 `chore` — build process, tooling, dependencies
- ⚡️ `perf` — performance improvement
- 👷 `ci` — CI/CD changes
- 🚧 `wip` — work in progress

## Summary line rules

- Imperative mood: "add login page" not "added login page"
- No period at the end
- 50 characters or fewer (hard limit: 72)
- Lowercase after the colon

## Body

- Wrap at 72 characters
- Explain **why**, not what — the diff shows what changed
- Separate from summary with a blank line

## Examples

```
✨ feat(auth): add OAuth2 login support

🐛 fix(bash): resolve PATH not exported in non-login shells

♻️ refactor(vscode): extract keybindings into separate template
```

## No sudo access

Assume Docker runs in **rootless mode**. There is no `sudo` access. Do not use `sudo` in any commands or suggest commands that require root privileges.
